# Hooks System

## Hook Types

- **PreToolUse**: Before tool execution (validation, parameter modification, can block via exit 1)
- **PostToolUse**: After tool execution (auto-format, checks, analysis)
- **Stop**: When session ends (final verification)

## Active Hooks

### PreToolUse
- tmux reminder for long-running commands
- git push review pause
- doc file blocker (prevents unnecessary .md/.txt creation)
- git commit security scan (blocks commits with secrets)

### PostToolUse
- Prettier auto-format for JS/TS files after edit
- TypeScript type check after editing .ts/.tsx
- console.log warning for edited files

### Stop
- console.log audit across all modified files

## Auto-Accept Permissions

- Enable for trusted, well-defined plans
- Disable for exploratory work
- Never use dangerously-skip-permissions flag
- Configure `allowedTools` in `~/.claude.json` instead
